---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Processing Pipeline
eyebrow: How it works
intro: "Thirteen stages, from raw input to a 3D scene. Expand any stage for details."
---
<div class="ribbon" style="margin-bottom:22px">
  {% for s in pipeline.stages %}<span class="node">{{ s.no }} {{ s.name }}</span>{% if not loop.last %}<span class="arr">→</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
</div>

{% for st in pipeline.stages %}
<details class="accordion" id="stage-{{ st.name | slug }}">
  <summary>
    <span><span class="stage-no">{{ st.no }}</span> <strong>{{ st.name }}</strong> <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400">· {{ st.purpose }}</span></span>
  </summary>
  <div class="body">
    <p>{{ st.details }}</p>
    <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:12px">
      <div><div class="mono-label">Inputs</div><ul style="margin-top:6px">{% for i in st.inputs %}<li>{{ i }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
      <div><div class="mono-label">Outputs</div><ul style="margin-top:6px">{% for o in st.outputs %}<li>{{ o }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul></div>
      <div><div class="mono-label">Tech</div><div class="tags" style="margin-top:8px">{% for t in st.tech %}<span class="badge cyan">{{ t }}</span>{% endfor %}</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</details>
{% endfor %}

<div class="callout" style="margin-top:24px">
  <div class="c-title">Note</div>
  <p>Heavy stages (depth, segmentation, pose, reconstruction) are interval-scheduled and cached rather than run on every frame, so the live path stays real-time. See <a href="{{ '/technology/#performance' | url }}">performance optimizations</a>.</p>
</div>
